Live round 2 fix (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): turning a frame-generation quality key on no longer stalls the frame thread.
- 0123 made each _extras twin pipeline on its first use: the first pair after a quality key (or the fill) was turned on
  held the frame thread 369-824 ms (synthesis_pair slow step at +0.4..+1.6 s in live round 2).
- With DCS's motion vectors on the NVIDIA backend (dcs_motion_enabled) and every key off at creation, the first pair that
  needs a twin (a quality key or the fill turned on from all off) starts a background build of every registered twin
  (start_extras_build: one below-normal thread, its own references to the device, root signatures and descriptions);
  nothing is built before. A pair that needs a twin
  not made yet composes with the plain pipeline and asks for that twin next (urgent), so a key takes effect a pair or
  two later and never waits on the frame thread. finish_extras_build joins the thread once it has ended (per pair: a
  null check and an atomic load). A rebuild leaves a running build to stop after its current pipeline; the destructor
  joins it. A synthesizer made with a key already on makes the twins at creation, as in 0123; without DCS motion they
  are still made on first use.
- Keys off for the whole session composes exactly as 0123 / 0.7.0: no twin is made or bound, no extra pipeline or driver
  memory. Once a key is turned on: a one-time background pipeline build (about 20 ms with the driver's shader cache warm;
  cold, the time 0123 spent on the frame thread, now off it) and the twins' pipeline objects held until the next rebuild
  (driver memory for at most 40 pixel-shader pipelines, estimated a few MB, not measured; no render targets or buffers).
- D3D12FrameSynthesizer::FgSettings: extras_building, extras_build_us, extras_binds.
- tests/fg_extras_async.inc (XRFG_TEST_FG_EXTRAS_ASYNC, label alone, NVIDIA hardware): a quality key turned on at the
  first pair (no build before it, none in the keys-off run); every submission timed on the calling thread against the same run with every key off (at most 5 ms
  more), and the twins bound within the run.

